Perch 2.0 INT8 backbone
Community derivative and release packaging by Benedict Carling, 2026.

Based on Perch 2.0, developed by Google Research and distributed under
Apache License 2.0. Original model:
https://www.kaggle.com/models/google/bird-vocalization-classifier/
Original source: https://github.com/google-research/perch
Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.04665

Perch 2.0: The Bittern Lesson for Bioacoustics
Bart van Merriënboer, Vincent Dumoulin, Jenny Hamer, Lauren Harrell,
Andrea Burns, Tom Denton.

Changes include a PyTorch backbone reconstruction, static INT8 QDQ
quantisation, explicit Pad constants for Neural-ART compatibility,
a NumPy inference frontend and release examples/documentation.
This is not an official Google or STMicroelectronics release.

example.wav and synthetic_reference.npz contain procedurally generated
signals, not third-party field recordings, and are covered by LICENSE.
Benchmark recordings and calibration recordings are not redistributed.
